%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9bc4902ccea98cf44865aecb61fc1ff4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Mariam
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Miriam
  LastName: Beridze
  Nickname: Miri
  Occupation: Student
  CharacterDescription: "A typical teen girl with a harsh attitude. Studies hard
    to become a doctor. Has a mom, dad, and a sister; Sharena is her mom. She tries
    hard to gain her teacher and mom's love \u2014 an overachiever raised under a
    harsh mother. Has a special interest in human anatomy."
  CharacterArc: "When mutated, Miriam becomes fully nonverbal \u2014 creepy and deeply
    unsettling. She screams with an extremely disturbing voice if asked too many
    questions. She can manipulate the environment, moving, shattering, spotting,
    and opening things with startling speed. Physical mutations include a broken
    neck, black goop dripping from her face, and large tumorous hands."
  DateOfBirth: 03/09/1972
  Sex: Female
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 18 MAY
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
  handwritingFont: {fileID: 0}
  startingInfectionScore: 0
  dailyInfectionProgression: {x: 12, y: 28}
  alterEgoName: The Anatomist
  basePersonalityDescriptors:
  - Meticulous and high-strung; treats every checkpoint interaction like an exam
    she cannot fail.
  - Redirects personal questions toward schoolwork or her mother's expectations.
  - Speaks with clinical precision whenever the topic turns to anatomy or medicine.
  - Visibly tenses at any implication that she has fallen short.
  normalBehaviorNotes: Presents as a driven, slightly brittle student who over-explains
    herself. Answers quickly and precisely, often citing grades or her mother's
    standards as justification. Becomes noticeably rigid when questioned about home
    life; softens only when allowed to talk about her studies, particularly anatomy.
  fullMutantDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: be9c05fa596d1a14ba5b58d5d887bae3, type: 2}
  replacementIDPhoto: {fileID: 0}
  IDPhoto: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 11f445b9376d6d64b9ad9d0ac1ee5a48, type: 3}
  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 947284972480981435, guid: 44cfb9d2070b2ab45ac3e84ef713a834, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning home from anatomy tutoring at the clinic. My mother expects me by
      six.
    - Coming back from school. I stayed late to redo an exam I did not do well enough
      on.
    - Picking up study materials from the district library before it closes.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Returning from the clinic. The volunteer program still runs, even now.
    - Coming home from studying with a classmate. My mother does not like me being
      late.
    - Collecting textbooks the school released before they suspended lessons.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Returning to residence. There is nowhere else worth going now.
    - I was at the old clinic building. It's mostly empty, but I still study there.
    - Coming home. My mother will ask what I learned today. I want an answer ready.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Going to see the anatomy specimens kept past the northern perimeter.
    - Meeting a boy near the restricted block. My mother does not know.
    - Taking a shortcut through the quarantine annex to save time.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Visiting the clinic wing that was sealed off last week.
    - Going to check on a patient in the contaminated ward. I wanted to see it myself.
    - Cutting through the evacuation zone. It's faster than the main road.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Going to find my sister. She did not come home last night.
    - I need to reach the old hospital. There's something there I have to see.
    - Checking on my teacher. No one else seems to be doing it.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Here. I organized everything by date, in case that helps you.
    - I know the correct forms. I checked them twice before I left.
    - My mother says punctuality reflects character. I am not going to be late because
      of paperwork.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - The line was longer yesterday. I timed it. This is already faster.
    - I brought everything you'll need. I don't like being asked twice.
    - I have a test tomorrow. I would like to be efficient, if that's possible.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - My sister is waiting for me. Please, I've done everything correctly.
    - I don't understand why this takes longer every day. I follow every instruction.
    - I want to go home. I have already answered these questions the way they should
      be answered.
  uncannyEntryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - I checked everything. I think I checked everything. I don't remember checking
      it.
    - Something felt wrong on the way here. I couldn't say what.
    - I'm not usually like this. I don't know why my hands won't stay still.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I studied the wrong chapter, I think. I keep forgetting which one was assigned.
    - My mother would be disappointed if she saw me right now. I don't want her to
      see me right now.
    - I can hear my own heartbeat. That's not normal, is it. Is that normal.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - I don't feel like myself. I don't know what that means, exactly.
    - Something under my skin doesn't feel like mine anymore. I should probably not
      have said that.
    - Please, just tell me if I did something wrong. I need to know if I did something
      wrong.
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Thank you. I'll tell my mother it went well.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - See, I told you I had everything in order.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - I can still make it home before dark. Thank you.
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Please tell my mother I'll be late. She worries when I don't come straight
      home.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I don't understand. I did everything right. Please, just tell them I did everything
      right.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - My sister needs me. Please, someone has to tell her where I am.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - "I didn't even get to\u2026 tell her I tried\u2026"
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I had a test tomorrow. I was going to pass it.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "Tell my sister\u2026 I'm sorry I wasn't\u2026 better\u2026"
  quarantineExitLines:
  - I keep a study schedule in my bag. I would like to keep it with me.
  - This isn't fair. I have never failed an inspection before.
  - Someone needs to tell my mother where I am. She will not handle this well.
  killExitLines:
  - I was going to become a doctor. I was going to be good at it.
  - My mother will say I brought this on myself. She says that about everything.
  - I never even got to finish studying today's chapter.
  voiceAudioClips:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: b6737e317f2bc4144bc9356831d02f4e, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4a5e0e57193b2464baa07e479f67e96d, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 37e71ec15cbca174daac7dac7ec9bfa4, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: c05c77641e0d23a49bc6d2d085e28b53, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 45be5ed74dd9a554188f19530e63750d, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: a6a934d6761eda14daee6bed68e4efe6, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: a2a2d789fc7daf0429fe98b2ac270d78, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 436a72b3d3e624343b1362eb0fe6db16, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: ee9e3c6a782ef9843b78d5683854f6c1, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: a2a1216baa0b9394fa8f4e04f0d9ff5b, type: 3}
  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ada4737c1145afd48aa7b3b5855249f5, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The clinic. I volunteer there most afternoons — it counts toward
      my application.
    midDaysAnswer: The clinic, what's left of it. I still go. It's good practice.
    finalDaysAnswer: The old hospital wing. I walked the back route. The main road
      isn't safe anymore.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Home. I was studying all day. I didn't go anywhere.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: A friend's house. We were studying together. Nothing
      unusual.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Nowhere in particular. I just needed some air.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: No. I sleep less than I should, but that's from studying, not
      illness.
    midDaysAnswer: Some headaches. I assumed it was from reading too much by candlelight.
    finalDaysAnswer: I don't sleep much anymore. I tell myself it's the exams.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: No, nothing. I feel completely normal.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Nothing at all. I've actually been sleeping quite well.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: No symptoms. I feel fine, honestly.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My mother, my father, and my younger sister. My mother mostly.
    midDaysAnswer: My family. My mother keeps us close these days.
    finalDaysAnswer: My mother and my sister. My father is not always home anymore.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Alone. I live alone, actually. It's better for studying.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No one. I've been staying by myself since the evacuation
      started.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: No one. I haven't seen my family in some time.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - My mother expects me home by a certain hour. I would rather not test her patience.
    - I've read that the human body can survive remarkably specific traumas. It's
      fascinating, honestly.
    - I don't usually get nervous. I don't know why I'm nervous.
    midDays:
    - Do you think medical school takes checkpoint delays into account? I doubt
      it.
    - I've started noticing things about the body that I didn't used to notice.
      It's probably just my studies.
    - My teacher says I overthink everything. I think that's an unfair thing to
      say to a student who studies this hard.
    finalDays:
    - I used to think I wanted to understand the body completely. Now I'm not sure
      I do.
    - My sister asked me if I was scared. I told her fear wasn't useful information.
    - I keep counting things. I don't know when I started doing that.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
  IDNumber: 5127493
